WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.963
[crowd cheering] Paris! Paris!
Paris! Paris! Paris! Paris! Paris!

00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:10.030
I've given my whole life to everyone for so long.

00:00:12.553 --> 00:00:15.181
It's just been really important
to me to keep this a secret.

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:16.307
Let’s wash our hands.

00:00:19.143 --> 00:00:23.314
It's just the first time that something is just mine.

00:00:26.108 --> 00:00:28.027
I’m gonna be a mom.

00:00:28.182 --> 00:00:29.600
Literally no one knows.

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:31.644
My own family doesn't know.

00:00:31.644 --> 00:00:37.442
Ever since I've been mic’d all I have done
is say the most terrible things. Oops!

00:00:37.442 --> 00:00:41.237
If people found out, there would
be paparazzi all over Cedars.

00:00:42.399 --> 00:00:44.067
I got you a surprise.

00:00:44.491 --> 00:00:45.033
This is your

00:00:45.033 --> 00:00:46.326
grandson, Phoenix.

00:00:46.326 --> 00:00:47.543
Are you serious?

00:00:47.611 --> 00:00:49.113
Yeah.

00:00:49.541 --> 00:00:50.409
What is that?

00:00:50.409 --> 00:00:51.960
Is that a... real?

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:53.427
Yes!

00:00:55.718 --> 00:00:58.262
He’s so beautiful, so perfect.

00:00:58.262 --> 00:01:00.681
My life is finally complete.

00:01:00.681 --> 00:01:01.891
I’m so obsessed.

00:01:02.411 --> 00:01:02.745
(Gasp!)

00:01:02.911 --> 00:01:03.745
He’s peeing.

00:01:03.745 --> 00:01:04.621
Oh no!

00:01:04.621 --> 00:01:07.665
Oh! Hahahaha! That’s hot!

00:01:07.665 --> 00:01:10.084
Have you talked to your mom about the book?

00:01:10.244 --> 00:01:12.454
It's just not an easy subject.

00:01:12.944 --> 00:01:17.574
Writing this book was one of the most
difficult experiences of my life.

00:01:17.574 --> 00:01:21.077
Writing about things that I've never told anyone.

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:22.438
No!

00:01:22.575 --> 00:01:24.702
I was just embarrassed and scared.

00:01:25.054 --> 00:01:27.056
The fact that you couldn't come to us.

00:01:27.526 --> 00:01:30.947
And we had to read about it online and in a book.

00:01:30.947 --> 00:01:34.158
It's not right for us to just
read about it in the media.

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:36.873
What's your best advice?

00:01:36.873 --> 00:01:38.417
It's not taking that job.

00:01:38.417 --> 00:01:39.669
I don't want to leave him.

00:01:39.669 --> 00:01:42.630
They’re this small for such a small window.

00:01:42.630 --> 00:01:43.590
It's hard to say, “no.”

00:01:43.590 --> 00:01:44.507
But you’re greedy.

00:01:45.104 --> 00:01:46.189
Like, you’re very greedy.

00:01:46.189 --> 00:01:48.399
No, I just like to work hard.

00:01:48.836 --> 00:01:55.551
People who are trauma victims have a very
hard time happily bonding with their children.

00:01:58.744 --> 00:02:03.790
[crowd cheering] Paris! Paris!
Paris! Paris! Paris!

00:02:05.652 --> 00:02:07.111
Sliving.

00:02:13.057 --> 00:02:16.352
Did you just fart on me?

